00:08:14,159 --> 00:08:26,320
 From the book, I learned that one of the reasons why Doom was so successful was because the company made themselves a map editor called Doom Editing Utilities.

74
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:30,000
 This was a pivotal tool in the creation of the game.

75
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:39,520
 This editor allowed designers to create, modify, and visualize the game's levels in a more interactive and efficient manner than previously.

76
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:46,400
 This is why the levels of the game were so good, because designers were able to iterate efficiently.

77
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:53,439
 Before graphical editors like this, game developers often had to manually code levels using text files.

78
00:08:53,440 --> 00:09:03,000
 This process involved specifying coordinates, object placements, and other level details in the text editor, which was both time consuming and error prone.

79
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:07,720
 Without a visual interface, developers could not see their changes real time.

80
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:14,760
 They had to compile and run the game to see the results of their edits, making the design process really, really slow.

