00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:08,000
 We usually think of design systems as a library of components, but once you get into the code implementation, it really all comes down to token definitions.

94
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:20,560
 In the context of design systems, tokens are standardized reusable variables that store the visual design attributes such as colors, typography, spacing, and other stylistic elements.

95
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:32,400
 These tokens act as the single source of truth for design specifications, ensuring consistency and uniformity across different components in the design system library.

96
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:49,040
 So if we can find a way to control the tokens, play with them and commit them to code, then we can make ourselves a design tool that lets us iterate fast on design while putting those changes straight into the code base.

